clear to your viewers.

00:22:12.864 --> 00:22:15.200 align:start size:88% position:13%
The most important
thing in life is wisdom.

00:22:15.200 --> 00:22:19.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good intentions don't mean
crap, may mean nothing.

00:22:19.071 --> 00:22:21.673
The amount of evil done by
people with good intentions

00:22:21.673 --> 00:22:25.010
is greater than the amount
of evil done by sadists.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:28.347 align:start position:0%
So if you think you're good
cause you have good intentions,

00:22:28.347 --> 00:22:33.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
join the list of people
who haven't done any good.

00:22:34.519 --> 00:22:35.854
You need wisdom to
make a better world

00:22:35.854 --> 00:22:39.024
and to make a better
character for yourself.

00:22:39.024 --> 00:22:44.029
These five books are wisdom
, about every aspect of life.

00:22:46.565 --> 00:22:51.336 align:start size:97% position:3%
I am so in love with the
Torah, the first five books.

00:22:51.336 --> 00:22:53.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
And thank God I
know them in Hebrew

00:22:53.071 --> 00:22:55.040 align:start size:97% position:3%
cause obviously I don't
think I could have done this

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:57.042
without knowing the Hebrew.

00:22:57.042 --> 00:22:59.644
I am so in love with it
that you'll find this,

00:22:59.644 --> 00:23:02.080
you who are making
your way gradually

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:06.651 align:start size:97% position:3%
to a less secular life,
you'll find this of interest.

00:23:06.651 --> 00:23:10.956
And I say this now
a lot in speeches.

00:23:12.391 --> 00:23:16.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't believe in the Torah
because I believe in God.

00:23:16.495 --> 00:23:19.431
I believe in God because
I believe in the Torah.

00:23:20.632 --> 00:23:23.535
My vehicle to belief
in God is rational.

00:23:23.535 --> 00:23:26.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's why my series is
called The Rational Bible.

00:23:26.905 --> 00:23:30.142
This is the third of
five of those books.

00:23:30.142 --> 00:23:33.912
My vehicle to God
is not miracles,

00:23:33.912 --> 00:23:36.982
is not visions, is not emotion.

00:23:36.982 --> 00:23:39.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is, and I'm not saying
everyone's vehicle,

00:23:39.317 --> 00:23:41.386
but mine is reason.

00:23:41.386 --> 00:23:46.324 align:start size:88% position:13%
The Torah is my
rational vehicle to God.

00:23:46.324 --> 00:23:51.329
And I make that case in
each of these volumes.

00:23:52.464 --> 00:23:55.033
So I gave you example
of those two laws.

00:23:55.033 --> 00:23:56.835
Here's another one. Let's see.

00:23:56.835 --> 00:23:58.570
Oh God, you shall, okay.

00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:01.673
The 10 Commandments is
repeated in Deuteronomy.

00:24:01.673 --> 00:24:05.777 align:start position:0%
God says it in Exodus and Moses
repeats it in Deuteronomy.

00:24:05.777 --> 00:24:09.815
And Deuteronomy means
in Greek, second law.

00:24:09.815 --> 00:24:12.184 align:start size:84% position:16%
So this is Moses
reviewing everything.

00:24:13.652 --> 00:24:17.088
So one of them is, of course,
you shall have no other gods.

00:24:17.088 --> 00:24:20.258
And I point out in both
Exodus and Deuteronomy,

00:24:20.258 --> 00:24:25.263 align:start size:97% position:3%
we have more gods today
than any ancient pagan had.

00:24:26.131 --> 00:24:27.165
When you think of the false gods

00:24:27.165 --> 00:24:29.034
that people believe in today,

00:24:29.034 --> 00:24:31.403
you know, and I go through them.

00:24:31.403 --> 00:24:33.905
Like just one example, science.

00:24:33.905 --> 00:24:35.140
I believe in science.

00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:37.209
And I go, what the
hell does that mean?

00:24:37.209 --> 00:24:39.311
Does science tell
you to be kind?

00:24:39.311 --> 00:24:41.246
Does science tell
you to be honest?

00:24:41.246 --> 00:24:42.914
Does science tell you to marry?

00:24:42.914 --> 00:24:45.016 align:start size:84% position:16%
Does science tell
you to have children?

00:24:45.016 --> 00:24:47.953 align:start size:84% position:16%
Does science tell
you to be courageous?

00:24:47.953 --> 00:24:50.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
Science tells you nothing.
It tells you science.

00:24:50.188 --> 00:24:52.724
- You can also ask
the science people,

00:24:52.724 --> 00:24:53.892
they believe in science.

00:24:53.892 --> 00:24:55.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then ask them if
boys can become girls

00:24:55.527 --> 00:24:57.429
and they get quiet real quick.

00:24:57.429 --> 00:25:00.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
- That's right.
That's exactly right.

00:25:00.432 --> 00:25:01.700
Exactly right.

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:02.934
This was science.

00:25:02.934 --> 00:25:06.137
It was science not to
have kids in school.

00:25:06.137 --> 00:25:09.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
Sweet had kids in school every
single day, not one died.

00:25:09.774 --> 00:25:13.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
That wasn't science, that
was scared scientists

00:25:13.612 --> 00:25:15.580
who were worthless and harmful.

00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:17.015
- So do you connect that-

00:25:17.015 --> 00:25:19.751 align:start position:0%
- There's a big difference
between scientists and science.

00:25:19.751 --> 00:25:22.220
- So do you connect that to
what we talked about earlier,

00:25:22.220 --> 00:25:24.890
that in a weird way,
people need to believe

00:25:24.890 --> 00:25:26.825 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether they
believe that or not.

00:25:26.825 --> 00:25:29.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that whether they
think they have to or not,

00:25:29.060 --> 00:25:30.762 align:start size:84% position:16%
they end up believing
in something.

00:25:30.762 --> 00:25:34.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thus the secularists
just, or the progressives,

00:25:34.065 --> 00:25:35.534
whatever you wanna call them,

00:25:35.534 --> 00:25:37.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
they just pick the different
set of beliefs, period.

00:25:37.469 --> 00:25:39.604
- That is exact. Yes, exactly.

00:25:39.604 --> 00:25:43.174 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, Mother Earth, I
don't believe in Mother Earth.

00:25:43.174 --> 00:25:45.677 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I believe the earth
was created by God

00:25:45.677 --> 00:25:47.212
for humans to use.

00:25:47.212 --> 00:25:49.514
Not abuse, but use, okay?

00:25:49.514 --> 00:25:51.750 align:start size:84% position:16%
Humans are more
important than trees,

00:25:51.750 --> 00:25:53.451
more important than apes.

00:25:53.451 --> 00:25:58.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is my human centered,
divinely given belief.

00:25:59.324 --> 00:26:00.525
That's just another example.

00:26:00.525 --> 00:26:02.827
So which do you believe?

00:26:02.827 --> 00:26:04.963
Are the humans a curse on earth

00:26:04.963 --> 00:26:09.200
or are the humans
to control earth

00:26:12.070 --> 00:26:14.973 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the good of
the human species?

00:26:14.973 --> 00:26:16.207
I believe the latter.

00:26:18.176 --> 00:26:19.678
Yes, go on.

00:26:19.678 --> 00:26:21.012
- Well, do you sense that
over the last couple years,

00:26:21.012 --> 00:26:22.881
because of the COVID craziness

00:26:22.881 --> 00:26:24.616 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the way our
politics has become,

00:26:24.616 --> 00:26:26.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, cult-like,
or whatever,

00:26:26.685 --> 00:26:30.121
that people are waking up
to something more rational.

00:26:30.121 --> 00:26:31.523
Maybe they're not saying,

00:26:31.523 --> 00:26:33.325
okay, I'm ready to make
that leap of faith yet,

00:26:33.325 --> 00:26:34.593
a certain set of people,

00:26:34.593 --> 00:26:37.028 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that there is
something happening.

00:26:37.028 --> 00:26:38.396
You know, it's like if
you're gonna tell people

00:26:38.396 --> 00:26:39.631
that their sons are
their daughters,

00:26:39.631 --> 00:26:41.466
they might go, you know,

00:26:41.466 --> 00:26:43.201 align:start size:84% position:16%
maybe some of that
old stuff in the Torah

00:26:43.201 --> 00:26:45.870
or some of those other
old books is pretty good.

00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:50.075
- If they're exposed to
it, which is my dream.

00:26:50.075 --> 00:26:52.210
I have 4,000 reviews.

00:26:52.210 --> 00:26:54.179
By the way, when
"Exodus" came out,

00:26:54.179 --> 00:26:56.948
it was the number
two book on Amazon,

00:26:56.948 --> 00:27:01.886
which is astonishing for a
Bible commentary, you know?

00:27:03.054 --> 00:27:04.255
- Why do you write them
in a different order?

00:27:05.457 --> 00:27:09.461
- I be totally honest, I
wrote them in the order

00:27:09.461 --> 00:27:13.798
that I thought would appeal to
people to get them involved.

00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:15.900
If I started with Deuteronomy,

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:18.036
nobody would know what
the hell I was doing.

00:27:18.036 --> 00:27:19.671
But everybody heard of Exodus

00:27:19.671 --> 00:27:21.873
and everybody heard of Genesis.

00:27:21.873 --> 00:27:25.176
So I started with the two
most widely known books.

00:27:25.176 --> 00:27:27.112
And I'm working my way through.

00:27:27.112 --> 00:27:28.580
I mean, when I get to Leviticus,

00:27:28.580 --> 00:27:31.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you asked the average,
I believe this truly.

00:27:31.483 --> 00:27:35.086
If you went on Harvard
campus and said to a kid,

00:27:35.086 --> 00:27:38.356
Hey, do you know
what Leviticus is?

00:27:38.356 --> 00:27:39.791
He would probably say no.

00:27:39.791 --> 00:27:43.328
I said, well, Leviticus
is the favorite horse

00:27:43.328 --> 00:27:44.996
in the Kentucky Derby?

00:27:44.996 --> 00:27:46.831
They go, no kidding.

00:27:46.831 --> 00:27:48.366
- They love Leviticus.

00:27:48.366 --> 00:27:50.368
- Yeah Leviticus.

00:27:50.368 --> 00:27:53.104
Oh man, Leviticus fan Club.

00:27:53.104 --> 00:27:55.106
- Win the Triple Crown.

00:27:55.106 --> 00:27:56.675
Wait, I wanna back up to,

00:27:56.675 --> 00:27:58.443
as I've jotted down
a couple notes here,

00:27:58.443 --> 00:28:00.512
I usually don't have to jot
down notes for an interview,

00:28:00.512 --> 00:28:01.746
much less with a friend.

00:28:01.746 --> 00:28:03.181 align:start size:81% position:19%
But there's so
much going on here

00:28:03.181 --> 00:28:05.550 align:start size:88% position:13%
that I actually did
write a few things down.

00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:08.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
And obviously, you do this all
the time on your radio show

00:28:08.887 --> 00:28:11.823 align:start size:97% position:3%
and everywhere else, you
talk about goodness so much.

00:28:11.823 --> 00:28:14.292
And you connect that
really to the Torah,

00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:17.896
that it's not just knowledge
or wisdom as you would put it,

00:28:17.896 --> 00:28:20.131 align:start size:84% position:16%
but goodness is
also baked in there.

00:28:20.131 --> 00:28:22.801
and it doesn't seem like we
have a lot of that right now.

00:28:24.369 --> 00:28:28.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So my underlying belief
and that of the Torah

00:28:28.273 --> 00:28:31.209
is that God wants
people to be good.

00:28:31.209 --> 00:28:33.478
That is why, and it's
one of the reasons

00:28:33.478 --> 00:28:35.413
that I am in love
with the Torah,

00:28:35.413 --> 00:28:38.616 align:start size:84% position:16%
it makes clear you
don't have to be a Jew

00:28:38.616 --> 00:28:40.518
for God to reward you.

00:28:40.518 --> 00:28:43.054
You can be a pagan, you can be,

00:28:43.054 --> 00:28:46.791
obviously they didn't exist
then, but later a Christian,

00:28:46.791 --> 00:28:48.626
you could be anything.

00:28:48.626 --> 00:28:52.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
God judges your behavior,
not your theology.

00:28:52.030 --> 00:28:55.867
And that is one of
the greatest lessons.

00:28:55.867 --> 00:28:57.502
It's called ethical monotheism.

00:28:57.502 --> 00:29:00.138
It is my fundamental belief.

00:29:00.138 --> 00:29:03.541 align:start size:97% position:3%
If one wants to become a Jew,
one is more than welcome.

00:29:03.541 --> 00:29:05.009 align:start size:81% position:19%
But the Jewish
belief is not that

00:29:05.009 --> 00:29:07.345
you have to be a
Jew to be saved.

00:29:07.345 --> 00:29:09.147
You have to be a good person.

00:29:09.147 --> 00:29:11.983
Nobody is perfect. I
said good, not perfect.

00:29:11.983 --> 00:29:16.788
God made us flawed. And so we
have to do the best we can.

00:29:16.788 --> 00:29:20.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
You wanna do the best you
can, you have to learn wisdom.

00:29:20.325 --> 00:29:23.094 align:start size:88% position:13%
You can't be a good
person if you're a fool.

00:29:23.094 --> 00:29:27.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the basic
fundamental understanding.

00:29:27.065 --> 00:29:30.201 align:start size:97% position:3%
And in order to gain wisdom,
you have to study wisdom.

00:29:30.201 --> 00:29:32.670
That's why I wrote a
column a few weeks ago.

00:29:32.670 --> 00:29:34.339
I had more wisdom,

00:29:34.339 --> 00:29:37.575
and so did all the kids
in my class at Yeshiva,

00:29:37.575 --> 00:29:41.479
than 90% of today's
college professors.

00:29:41.479 --> 00:29:46.484 align:start size:84% position:16%
Again, when I was
15, I had more wisdom

00:29:47.652 --> 00:29:49.354
and so did my other
Yeshiva classmates

00:29:49.354 --> 00:29:52.891
and so did Christian kids in
traditional Christian schools

00:29:52.891 --> 00:29:57.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
than 90% of the professors
in America today.

00:29:57.028 --> 00:29:59.998 align:start size:81% position:19%
We studied wisdom,
we understood.

00:29:59.998 --> 00:30:02.700
For example, we knew
that people's nature

00:30:02.700 --> 00:30:04.302
is not basically good.

00:30:04.302 --> 00:30:07.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the average
professor probably thinks

00:30:07.572 --> 00:30:09.240
human nature is basically good,

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:11.342 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is the beginning
of foolishness.

00:30:11.342 --> 00:30:13.978
You can't have a
coherent worldview

00:30:13.978 --> 00:30:17.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you think human nature
is essentially good.

00:30:17.081 --> 00:30:19.918
- Is that also why
politics is so screwy

00:30:19.918 --> 00:30:21.853
that we have a bunch of people

00:30:21.853 --> 00:30:24.756
who just wanna take advantage
of people who are not wise?

00:30:24.756 --> 00:30:26.658
I mean, if you just turn on,

00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:27.826
you turn on almost,
almost anything,

00:30:27.826 --> 00:30:28.760
and it's like, man,

00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:30.428
you'd have to be pretty unwise

00:30:30.428 --> 00:30:32.297
to be buying any
of this nonsense

00:30:32.297 --> 00:30:34.732
from mainstream
media these days.

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:37.101
- Yeah, well, but the point is

00:30:37.101 --> 00:30:39.637 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's the unwise
leading the unwise.

00:30:39.637 --> 00:30:43.741 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's not like they're wise and
they're fooling the unwise.

00:30:43.741 --> 00:30:46.177
Is Gavin Newsom a wise man?

00:30:46.177 --> 00:30:47.979
- My audience knows my feelings.

00:30:47.979 --> 00:30:50.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Is Lori Lightfoot
a wise woman?

00:30:50.882 --> 00:30:55.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, but wisdom is
invalued, it isn't taught.

00:30:55.086 --> 00:30:59.791 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's why these books
that I'm writing,

00:30:59.791 --> 00:31:02.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think are so
incredibly important.

00:31:02.093 --> 00:31:05.163 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, nobody writes a Bible
commentary to get rich.

00:31:05.163 --> 00:31:09.868
I'm writing it because this is
my legacy of my life's work.

00:31:09.868 --> 00:31:12.303
People need to understand

00:31:12.303 --> 00:31:14.439
the greatest five
books ever written.

00:31:14.439 --> 00:31:15.707
And that's what this project

00:31:15.707 --> 00:31:17.041
is called, "The Rational Bible".

00:31:17.041 --> 00:31:18.343 align:start size:81% position:19%
