00:34:40.711 --> 00:34:42.480
- That's even better.

00:34:42.480 --> 00:34:45.249
Let's dive into a couple
of the other pieces here.

00:34:45.249 --> 00:34:48.986
Chapter 13 is Why
would God test us?

00:34:48.986 --> 00:34:50.221
This is obviously one

00:34:50.221 --> 00:34:52.523 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you've been asked
in a million forums

00:34:52.523 --> 00:34:55.393
on every probably radio
show you've ever done.

00:34:55.393 --> 00:34:56.627
Why would God...

00:34:56.627 --> 00:34:58.062
Shouldn't things just
be a little bit easier?

00:34:58.062 --> 00:35:00.031
Come on, there's
God, he's moral.

00:35:00.031 --> 00:35:01.466
We're trying to be good.

00:35:01.466 --> 00:35:03.935 align:start size:97% position:3%
Couldn't he just take it
easy on us just a little bit?

00:35:03.935 --> 00:35:06.337
Why do bad things happen
to good people, Dennis?

00:35:07.638 --> 00:35:10.641
- Well, those are two
separate questions,

00:35:10.641 --> 00:35:13.611 align:start size:97% position:3%
bad things happening to
good people and testing us.

00:35:13.611 --> 00:35:16.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't regard all
suffering as a divine test

00:35:16.514 --> 00:35:19.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it will imply that
if your kid has cancer,

00:35:19.951 --> 00:35:21.419
God gave your kid cancer.

00:35:21.419 --> 00:35:24.555
And I don't believe
that for a second.

00:35:24.555 --> 00:35:29.026
God created a world where
bad things can happen.

00:35:29.026 --> 00:35:33.231
And my best answer to
this question which is

00:35:33.231 --> 00:35:37.568
I've been absorbed with all
of my life since high school.

00:35:37.568 --> 00:35:42.206
I heard a statement from
a rabbi Milton Steinberg.

00:35:42.206 --> 00:35:46.978 align:start position:0%
And I think he said it, I didn't
hear it from him directly.

00:35:46.978 --> 00:35:49.147
I read it. I love it.

00:35:49.147 --> 00:35:50.414
He said the following,

00:35:51.616 --> 00:35:55.753 align:start size:88% position:13%
"the believer in God has
to explain one thing,

00:35:56.921 --> 00:36:01.559
the existence of
unjust suffering.

00:36:02.760 --> 00:36:05.563
The atheist has to explain

00:36:05.563 --> 00:36:08.032
the existence of
everything else."

00:36:09.433 --> 00:36:13.871 align:start position:0%
I find that the best answer
I've ever heard to this problem.

00:36:13.871 --> 00:36:16.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't deny it's a
problem, unjust suffering.

00:36:16.174 --> 00:36:17.074
I don't deny it.

00:36:18.276 --> 00:36:22.580
But compared to what the
atheist has to explain,

00:36:22.580 --> 00:36:24.982
literally everything else,

00:36:24.982 --> 00:36:28.386
and for which he
has no explanation,

00:36:28.386 --> 00:36:33.157
then I'm back to belief
in God with my question.

00:36:33.157 --> 00:36:35.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And as they say,
we're in a multiverse,

00:36:35.593 --> 00:36:36.827
that's what they always say.

00:36:36.827 --> 00:36:38.896
We're in a multiverse,
anything's possible.

00:36:38.896 --> 00:36:41.165
- You're right.

00:36:41.165 --> 00:36:43.734
The only thing that's not
possible is a multiverse.

00:36:45.670 --> 00:36:48.606 align:start size:97% position:3%
- That must be what believing
in one God is all about.

00:36:48.606 --> 00:36:51.509
It just kind of keeps
you off the multiverse.

00:36:51.509 --> 00:36:54.679
- Listen, just remember this,

00:36:54.679 --> 00:36:59.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
and this should be a message
even to people like you.

00:37:00.885 --> 00:37:02.987
And it is, I know, cause
you're now thinking that

00:37:02.987 --> 00:37:05.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
maybe religion has
something important to say.

00:37:08.893 --> 00:37:13.898 align:start size:97% position:3%
There were very few outliers
during the COVID hysteria

00:37:15.666 --> 00:37:19.570
and almost all of them were
religious, Christian or Jew.

00:37:20.438 --> 00:37:23.774
That's not insignificant.

00:37:25.409 --> 00:37:27.545
If a place was gonna be open

00:37:28.980 --> 00:37:30.915
and most, by the way, most
synagogues and churches,

00:37:30.915 --> 00:37:33.451 align:start size:81% position:19%
I think failed
the test terribly.

00:37:33.451 --> 00:37:37.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
They succumbed to secular
irrational authority

00:37:37.788 --> 00:37:39.557
just like everybody else.

00:37:39.557 --> 00:37:42.927 align:start size:84% position:16%
But those institutions
