00:39:51.689 --> 00:39:53.858
But he does seem like
he wants to be loved.

00:39:55.826 --> 00:39:56.660
- Trump?

00:39:56.660 --> 00:39:58.162
- Yeah.

00:39:58.162 --> 00:40:00.931
- If there's one thing,
even his enemies have to,

00:40:00.931 --> 00:40:04.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
he loves to be loved
by his followers,

00:40:04.335 --> 00:40:09.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
but as a general rule,
Trump has disdain.

00:40:09.206 --> 00:40:10.574
- Oh, that's interesting.

00:40:10.574 --> 00:40:13.444 align:start size:97% position:3%
So you're making a
distinction between sort of

00:40:13.444 --> 00:40:14.845
someone who has, let's say,

00:40:14.845 --> 00:40:16.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
followers or supporters
that love them

00:40:16.514 --> 00:40:19.550 align:start position:0%
versus he's not going for
institutional love or something.

00:40:19.550 --> 00:40:21.485
I mean, that's kind
of whittling it down.

00:40:21.485 --> 00:40:22.319
But you think-

00:40:22.319 --> 00:40:23.154
- Yes or exactly.

00:40:23.154 --> 00:40:23.988
No, no, no.

00:40:26.090 --> 00:40:29.427
You could say Trump loves Trump,

00:40:29.427 --> 00:40:33.330
but that Trump does
what he does for love

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:38.335 align:start size:97% position:3%
given the swiftness with which
he will lash out at people.

00:40:39.470 --> 00:40:41.071 align:start size:84% position:16%
He's the last person
